div.p:
Considering that the impost known under the name of “peajes,” (tolls on the
                    public highways,) is the cause, to those who are subject to it, of detention and
                    injury, which weighs particularly on the poorer class of the population;

Considering that it is desirable to adjust, as early as possible, the collection
                    of taxes in such a manner as to facilitate the future establishment of the
                    complete liberty of interior commerce;

Considering, finally, that the effects which, by this law, are to be taxed, are
                    those which really make the most use of the roads, and should, therefore, supply
                    the means for their repair;
